      {
        "id": 51534,
        "name": "LCinn",
        "username": "LCinn",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lcinn/{size}/2659_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-01-15T15:36:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Uuuuuugh. I’m going to have to get this. It’s just so amazing. But with the heavy hit of the Sentinels kickstarter, and new Netrunner stuff coming out all the time, it does hurt a little.</p>\n<p>By the way, a tip for teaching someone else the game: play your cards first and open the first few beats, and let them pick the optimal counter attack. It allows them to grasp the purpose of the different attacks much quicker. Just move to closed plays when the other player feels comfortable doing so.</p>\n<p>I sort of question the wisdom of including that guy with the different bases as the intermediate character in the print and play, because getting a grasp of the bases is such an essential part of the game. Throwing out most of what the player knows as soon as they move on to intermediate seems a bit silly.</p>",
        "post_number": 28,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:25:11.728Z",
